# `power::ybase`

Admittance base of a per-unit system.

## Signature

```cpp
double power::ybase(const power::Base& base);
```

## What It Does

Returns `power / voltage^2`, the admittance in siemens that equals `1` per unit.

## Parameters

`base`
: The power and voltage bases.

## Returns

The admittance base in siemens.

## Errors

Throws `std::invalid_argument` for a base that is not positive and finite.

## Interpretation and Use

Divide an admittance in siemens by it to get per unit.

